## 3. Core Debugging Rules (Mandatory Compliance)

| Rule | Principle | Why | Reference |
|---|---|---|---|
| **D1** | **Reproduce first.** One fast, deterministic, non-interactive command that fails with the reported symptom. Cannot reproduce → `NEEDS_CONTEXT`. | A fix you cannot see fail and pass is a guess. | [01-reproduce-read-and-tools]({{ref_01}}) |
| **D2** | **Read the first real error.** Inspect the root exception in chained tracebacks and the first frame in workspace code; redact secrets (`<REDACTED>`). | Fixing the outer wrapper frame wastes time on the wrong line. | [01-reproduce-read-and-tools]({{ref_01}}) |
| **D3** | **One failure at a time, first one first.** Stop at the first failure and resolve it before inspecting downstream cascades. | Parallel fixes hide which change resolved what. | [01-reproduce-read-and-tools]({{ref_01}}) |
| **D4** | **Minimize and isolate.** Cut inputs/steps to the smallest failing case; diff since last green; run `git bisect` only in a disposable worktree. | The minimal failing case becomes the permanent regression test. | [02-isolate-and-hypothesize]({{ref_02}}) |
| **D5** | **3–5 ranked falsifiable hypotheses, one variable per probe.** Log `H1`..`H3` with prediction, probe, and `CONFIRMED` / `RULED OUT`. | Multiple simultaneous edits make results ambiguous. | [02-isolate-and-hypothesize]({{ref_02}}) |
| **D6** | **Fix the root cause, not the symptom.** Trace the bad value backwards caller-by-caller to its source and check the diff for sibling bugs. | Symptom patches move the bug and leave siblings intact. | [02-isolate-and-hypothesize]({{ref_02}}) |
| **D7** | **Smallest fix at the owning layer, inside task scope.** Place the fix per `{{clean_architecture_link}}`; no unrelated refactoring. | Wrong-layer fixes break again and bloat review. | [03-fix-escalate-and-report]({{ref_03}}) |
| **D8** | **Red-to-Green regression test.** Prove the test fails for the reported reason without the fix and passes with the fix (`{{unit_testing_link}}`). | Without a regression test, the defect returns silently. | [03-fix-escalate-and-report]({{ref_03}}) |
| **D9** | **Never green-wash.** No skipped/weakened tests, swallowed errors, fake fallbacks, loosened types, arbitrary sleeps/retries, or lint suppressions. | Green-washing hides the bug and removes the safety net. | [03-fix-escalate-and-report]({{ref_03}}) |
| **D10** | **Environment vs. code.** Unreachable DB/service, missing env var, unapplied migration/codegen, or stale lockfile → `BLOCKED`, never a code workaround. | Code workarounds for broken environments break everyone else. | [03-fix-escalate-and-report]({{ref_03}}) |
| **D11** | **Remove temporary instrumentation.** Tag temporary logs `[DEBUG-xxxx]` and prove zero leftovers with `rg -n` and the linter (`{{clean_code_link}}` `C3`). | Leftover debug logs leak data and clutter output. | [02-isolate-and-hypothesize]({{ref_02}}) |
| **D12** | **Time-box (3 attempts) and escalate.** Stop after 3 failed fix attempts (`BLOCKED`); route contract/schema/dependency/scope changes to `change-control`. | Endless attempts burn context and violate approval gates. | [03-fix-escalate-and-report]({{ref_03}}) |
| **D13** | **Use non-interactive tracing tools.** Use code intelligence / `rg -n` for caller and impact tracing (`EXTEND` vs `INIT`); never run interactive debuggers that hang CLI shells. | Static/CLI tracing is fast, repeatable, and non-blocking. | [01-reproduce-read-and-tools]({{ref_01}}) |
| **D14** | **Report the root-cause analysis.** Include the structured Debug Report block and Red/Green evidence rows in the hand-off. | Reviewers verify causal reasoning, not just the diff. | [03-fix-escalate-and-report]({{ref_03}}) |

